  "prefLabel": "En 1012.05 Scoping Meeting",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1012.05 Scoping Meeting.\n\n(a) The purpose of the scoping meeting shall be to discuss the application, the group, and review existing studies relevant to the application. At the scoping meeting, the utility shall provide pertinent information such as aggregate export capacity of all other facilities in the common study area, thermal limits of the substation transformer and distribution feeders, quantity of applications and aggregate export capacity of the facilities in the group, whether a substation transformer will need to be upgraded, and whether there are any additional system modification anticipated.\n\n(b) The utility shall conduct a scoping meeting with all group members with facilities in the common study area within 20 business days of the close of the group window.\n\n(c) The scoping meeting shall take place in person, by telephone, or electronically by a means mutually agreeable to the parties.\n\n(d) The utility and the applicant shall bring to the meeting personnel, including system engineers, and other resources as might be reasonably required to accomplish the purpose of the meeting.\n\n(e) By mutual agreement of the parties, the scoping meeting may be waived.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
